# /etc/portage/env — per-package fallback ladder
#
# The default flags in make.conf are the most aggressive tier. When a
# package fails to build or misbehaves, demote it ONE step at a time via
# /etc/portage/package.env. Changing to a more conservative tier is the
# last resort — first check whether the failure has a non-flag cause.
#
# Fallback ladder (least → most conservative):
#   (default)             make.conf: -Ofast + Polly + ThinLTO + unified-LTO
#                         + libc++ link set
#   no-polly.conf         default minus Polly/alignment        (1st fallback)
#   thin-lto-only.conf    default minus unified-LTO extras (vtable opts)
#   O3.conf               -O3 instead of -Ofast, no Polly, full LTO
#   O3-no-vtables.conf    O3.conf minus the vtable/unified extras
#   no-openmp.conf        -Ofast, no Polly/OpenMP/lib forcing, full LTO
#   no-lto.conf           default flags but LTO off (incl. Rust LTO)
#   no-link-libs.conf     default LTO but without the -l* lib forcing
#   O2.conf               plain -O2 -march=native + libc++ link set
#   plain.conf            plain -O2 -march=native, no ccache (true last resort)
#
# Toolchain / special-purpose:
#   gcc.conf              build with GCC instead of clang (GCC-valid flags)
#   glibc.conf            default minus the -Wno-* downgrade set
#   rust-llvm21.conf      dev-lang/rust: pin clang/llvm 21 toolchain
#   rust-no-lto.conf      conservative RUSTFLAGS/CFLAGS for broken cargo pkgs
#   no-ccache.conf        disable ccache (+sandbox relaxation)
#   no-extra-econf.conf   reset EXTRA_ECONF (--with-rocm) where it breaks
#   libstdcxx-headers.conf clang with explicit gcc-15 libstdc++ header paths
#   highway-noavx512.conf gcc + AVX512 disabled (dev-cpp/highway consumers)
#   include-string.conf   O3 + CXXFLAGS --include string (hyprland)
#   mount-defines.conf    extra -include/-D defines (xfsprogs)
#   gimp.conf, nvidia.conf, zfs-kernel.conf: package-specific
#
# Files in env/<category>/<package> are auto-sourced bashrc hooks
# (source patching etc.), independent of package.env.
